# Architecture — general

FSD-based layering. The directory is `N_<layer>`, the import alias is `~<layer>`, and the layer name is `<layer>` — the part after the underscore; the numeric prefix only sets import order. Example: `1_app` / `~app` / layer `app`.

Import flow, enforced by `eslint-plugin-boundaries`:

```
global → shared → core → entities → features → widgets → pages → app
```

A layer may import only layers to its right (lower in the flow). No cross-imports between slices of the same layer. Slice layers (pages, widgets, features, entities) are imported only via their `index.ts` public API.

Layer-by-layer definitions live in [`architecture/layers.mdc`](./layers.mdc). Segment contents (`api`/`model`/`domain`/`lib`/`ui`) live in [`architecture/segments.mdc`](./segments.mdc).

## Cross-cutting rules

- Import flow: `global → shared → core → entities → features → widgets → pages → app`; a layer imports only layers to its right.
- No cross-imports between slices of the same layer (pages, widgets, features, entities).
- Slice layers are imported only via their `index.ts` public API (`boundaries/entry-point`).
- The `domain` segment imports nothing.
- Full rules: [`/eslint/configs/boundaries/eslint.boundaries.config.ts`](/eslint/configs/boundaries/eslint.boundaries.config.ts).
